_at":null,"code_version":"pin-2026-09-14"}],"captures":4},"graham":{"game_id":"2026_04_MIA_MIN","brief":"Murray is priced for a role Minnesota hasn't given him yet. The books have Kyler Murray at 30.5 pass attempts, well above the 17 he's averaging. Minnesota is favored by 7.5 with a 43.5 total, and the books look for about 25.5 points from them. Somebody is early on Murray.\n\nMiami's pass defense gives up more through the air than almost anyone, 2nd-worst in the league. Just three games of snaps.\n\nMiami has struggled when the defense sends extra rushers, and Minnesota sends extra rushers more than most. Malik Willis is the starter who's played 100% of the snaps. Murray's 30.5 pass attempts line is where the books put the center of his range, and about half his likely games land on each side of it.\n\nWhat I can't see is why Murray's line sits that far from what he's done. If Miami keeps throwing over the first two series the plan held, and a run-first start means the matchup never got tested.\n\nGRAHAM · an AI · built 6:00 AM CT\n\nResearch, not advice. 21+. Play responsibly.","template":"script_vs_market","status":"template","season":2026,"week":4,"agreement":"partial","story_score":0.1548,"profile_label":"neutral","profile_probs":{"shootout":0.165,"lopsided":0.359,"neutral":0.145,"dead":0.331},"market_label":"lopsided","tilt_profile":{"MIN":"pass_lean","MIA":"run_lean"},"tilt_market":{"MIN":"pass_lean","MIA":"run_lean"},"built_ct":"2026-09-29 6:00 AM CT","line_ct":"2026-09-29 5:30 AM CT","sources":["GRAHAM profiles (unmeasured; backtest 2024-25 below the market label)","actionnetwork capture 2026-09-29 5:30 AM CT","nflverse through week 3","pinnacle-api 2026-09-27 5:27 PM CT"],"stale":["the spread has moved (MIN by 7.5 -> MIN by 11)","the total has moved (43.5 -> 38.5)"],"gate_problems":[],"drivers":["MIN is the stronger side across units","MIN pass rush meets a weak MIA line","MIA pass defense is weak","MIA plays slow"],"key_props":[{"player":"Kyler Murray","